module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.head_landed_by_hand_before_its_own_verification_reported

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data head_landed_by_hand_before_its_own_verification_reported: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "head_landed_by_hand_before_its_own_verification_reported" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a head reaches main while that head's own verification run is still in flight, so what lands carries no terminal verdict about itself.** INVALID STATE, AT THE GRAIN THAT WAS ACTUALLY OBSERVED: at the instant of the landing there exists no concluded run for the landed ref. WHAT THIS ROW DOES NOT CLAIM, because the evidence does not reach it: WHICH admission path permitted the landing -- an absent constraint, a constraint that treats an unreported required context as not-failing, or a bypass -- is a separate question, and the actor and the timestamps do not settle it. The class is the uncertified landing itself, which is observable from the record alone. ",

    "THIS ROW IS RANKED FIRST AND IT SUBSUMES THE DETECTION-TIMING CLASSES. If a head can reach main before its checks conclude, then no improvement to WHAT a check detects, HOW FAST it detects it, or WHICH lane it is routed to changes the outcome: the detector was correct and it was consulted after the fact. Any repair argued from detection quality is arguing below this row. ",

    "HARM: the break lands on main, where every other lane inherits it. The 2026-09-03 outage ran roughly eighty minutes -- main red from 19:49 UTC until #10278 (1af8892e143) deleted four lines -- and during it any lane resolving `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` could not regenerate its projection, so the blast radius was every concurrent lane touching a generated artifact, not the author's own branch. ",

    "**SPECIMEN, MEASURED (gunbc#10236, cfe19ea7f48, 2026-09-03).** The pull request's only CI run on its merged head was created at 19:49:40Z; the pull request merged at 19:49:43Z, THREE SECONDS later; that run concluded FAILURE at 20:30:34Z. The interval between the run beginning and the merge is shorter than any job in it takes to check out a tree, so no reading of the record can make the merge a decision taken on evidence. ",

    "**THE MERGE WAS PERFORMED BY A PERSON, AND THAT IS RECORDED AS AN OBSERVATION ABOUT THE ACTOR, NOT AS A MECHANISM.** `gh api` reports `merged_by: briansrls` on the merged pull request, so the landing was a human action rather than an automated queue advancing a ref. WHY THE ACTOR IS WORTH RECORDING AT ALL: it fixes WHO the repair has to reach -- a repair aimed at an automated arm changes nothing for a landing no automated arm performed, while a repair that puts the run before the landing reaches both. IT DOES NOT FOLLOW, AND THIS ROW DOES NOT SAY, THAT NOTHING STOOD BETWEEN THE ACTOR AND MAIN: that would be a claim about the admission path, and the next receipt keeps this filing's measurement apart from the repository's. ",

    "DISTINCT FROM `required_evidence_absent_reads_as_evidence_of_pass`, and the two are easily fused because they share a specimen. That row's subject is an ADMISSION ARM whose quantifier folds over the receipts that have arrived, so the empty enumeration admits -- a defect readable in the arm. This row's subject is the LANDING: a ref reached main with no terminal verdict of its own, whatever arm did or did not consider it. One names a wrong answer; the other names the state that answer produced, which is also reachable by paths that arm never touches. ",

    "**WHAT IS UNMEASURED HERE, AND WHAT IS MEASURED ELSEWHERE, KEPT APART ON PURPOSE.** THIS filing could not read the protection configuration -- branch protection is unreadable from a session token, `gh api` returning 403 -- so nothing below is my own measurement of the ruleset. WHAT THE REPOSITORY DOES RECORD, cited rather than re-derived: `gunbc.merge_lifecycle` holds that `gunbc.repo_ruleset` `desired_ruleset_rules` read ruleset 16178731 back with NO divergence -- active, default-branch-scoped, one required context -- and that the merge was admitted anyway, because the platform decides required contexts on what has REPORTED at the merge instant and a context that has not reported is `expected` rather than `failing`. So on that authority the answer to `was there a constraint` is YES AND IT ADMITTED, which is exactly why this row is written about the UNCERTIFIED LANDING and not about a missing gate. A reader with a token that can read protection can convert that citation into a first-hand measurement; until then this row asserts the landing and nothing about the ruleset, since treating it as ruleset evidence would be the fabrication DESIGN section 5 forbids. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: for a landed head, read two timestamps and one actor -- the terminal conclusion time of the run on THAT head, and the merge time. If the merge precedes the conclusion, the landing was uncertified regardless of what the run later said, and the actor tells you which of the two repairs applies. The record afterwards looks ordinary in both cases, because the run does eventually conclude and the conclusion is attached to a head that is already in history. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, and only by human habit -- the failure is contained after the fact by a repair pull request, and nothing structural stood between the decision and main. ",

    "**CEILING, AND THE ROW ANSWERS THE QUESTION IT WAS ASKED RATHER THAN ASSERTING A NUMBER: THE CEILING SPLITS BY PATH, AND THE CLASS TAKES THE MINIMUM.** DESIGN section 4b puts external reality OFF the ladder deliberately -- observed, refused or mitigated at a declared boundary, and explicitly not a fifth rung -- so `a merge queue would close this` is only a ceiling if the thing that would refuse is a path this repository CONSTRUCTS. It is not one path here, it is two. ",

    "PATH ONE, OURS AND ON THE LADDER: a landing taken through an admission decision this repository models. That decision exists -- `gunbc.merge_lifecycle` `merge_enabled` consulting `gunbc.merge_admission` `policy_admits`, with the absent-receipt case now an ARM of the decision rather than a fold seed -- so the invalid state is authorable, the refusal is authorable, and the RED is enrollable against it. CEILING ON THIS PATH: 3, structurally guaranteed, because no `Accepted` landing through our own path carries a head with no terminal verdict. It is not 4 while the same model can still represent a policy that admits one. ",

    "PATH TWO, NOT OURS AND OFF THE LADDER: a person pressing merge in the hosting platform. Nothing this repository constructs stands on that path, and the platform behaviour that would close it is observed, not authored -- `gunbc.repo_ruleset` `desired_ruleset_rules` reads ruleset 16178731 back with NO divergence while the merge still lands, because the platform decides required contexts on what has REPORTED at the merge instant, and a context that has not reported is `expected` rather than `failing`. The honest form on this path is therefore a BOUNDARY OBLIGATION and not a rung: declare the desired ruleset state, converge it, and OBSERVE every landing -- comparing the landed head against the terminal verdicts that existed at its merge instant -- refusing loudly when there were none. That observation is ours and can climb; the enforcement is not ours and cannot be claimed. Today even the observation is partial, because branch protection is unreadable from a session token, so the boundary is currently held by timestamps alone. ",

    "**SO THE ROW'S CEILING IS THE BOUNDARY OBLIGATION, WHICH IS THE MINIMUM ACROSS ITS IN-SCOPE PATHS**, per 4b(1): a class's rung is the minimum over the paths in scope, and this class's specimen is on the path we do not own. Claiming structural guarantee for the whole class on the strength of path one would be exactly the inflation 4b(1) names -- citing the strongest path while the one the incident happened on stays silent. What a merge queue changes is not that we PROVE anything; it is that path two stops existing, and the class collapses onto path one. That is a real repair and it is why the trigger still names it -- but until it is configured, this row is a declared boundary, and it says so. ",

    "RECORDED BECAUSE A READER WILL NOTICE IT: the sibling row `required_evidence_absent_reads_as_evidence_of_pass` states CEILING: structurally guaranteed on the same merge-queue construction. This row does not amend that one -- its subject is an admission arm, which is nearer to path one -- but the split above is the narrower reading, and a reader reconciling the two should reconcile them in that direction: the queue is a construction we can ADOPT, not one we can PROVE from here. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY AND IN TWO PARTS BECAUSE THE CEILING HAS TWO PATHS: `gunbc.guarantee_stall` `merge_admission_terminal_verdict_stall` -- (a) a landing path in which the verdict on the ref that lands is a PRECONDITION of the landing, sufficient to refuse a merge whose head carries no terminal conclusion, human actor included, which is what removes path two rather than measuring it; and (b) until that exists, a landing OBSERVATION over merged heads, sufficient to refuse when the landed head carried no terminal verdict at its merge instant, which is the declared boundary discharging its own obligation. The stall was ruled open by the operator on 2026-09-03 -- \"Leave the hole open for now - i know merging is not sound\" -- so (a) is held by ruling and not by omission, and (b) is what this row asks for meanwhile. A dashboard, a reminder, or a review convention does not discharge it: each leaves the same person the same three seconds.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
